{:name "daily-plan"
 :purpose "Turn the open intents into today's attempts, and surface the ones that have stalled: the owner's day, planned where the owner plans."
 :executor :agent
 :skill "../../.claude/skills/plan-day"
 :inputs {:intents {:status :open :horizon-within-days 14 :standing false}
          :events {:last-hours 24}}
 :procedure "Follow the plan-day skill, carried in full in the brief. In short: the brief's open intents are every open intent in the ledger with a horizon inside 14 days, the vault's and every other system's alike. For each, plan at most one attempt for today and name the spec it would run; flag any intent with no attempt in the last 7 days; keep the list short enough to finish. Record each item as one event into the attempt (plan/step, plan/flag), then end the attempt. Each step cites the events that support it or says it is untested, names what would refute it before looking, and reads a missing event as unknown, never as undone. Propose at most three intents per run with propose, each a closed question the owner answers with opened or dropped. When the window's events show an intent's criterion is satisfied, judge it met with those events as evidence: a draft the owner accepts or overrules, never a closed intent."
 :output {:plan/step {:intent :id :spec :string :note :string :evidence [:id]}
          :plan/flag {:intent :id :reason :string}}
 :criterion "By end of day, every accepted attempt has an ended timestamp and at least one event beyond start and end."
 :check {:query [:find ?e :in ?attempt :where (in-attempt ?e ?attempt) (or [?e :event/kind :plan/step] [?e :event/kind :plan/flag])]}
 :acts-on [:commitments]
 :trigger {:daily "07:00"}
 :budget {:minutes 10}}
